window.REPORT = {"updated":"2026-11-19","version":"0.1 — first assembly, research still landing","sections":[{"tab":"overview","kicker":"How to read this","title":"Two questions, thirty teams","title_zh":"兩個問題，三十支團隊","lede":"This report asks the same two questions of every team it looks at.","lede_zh":"本報告對每一支團隊都問同樣的兩個問題。","body":"The first question is computational. Where does a project stop being wet biology and start being a model, a pipeline, a dataset, a piece of software? What did that layer actually decide — did it change an experiment, or was it decoration added after the fact? The teams that win are increasingly the ones where the answer is \"it changed the experiment\".\n\nThe second question is social. Who outside the team touched this project, and what did they change about it? A list of meetings is not integrated human practices. A design that is visibly different because somebody outside the lab said something is.\n\nEverything else here — the trend tabs, the roadmap — exists to answer a third question that only GEMS Research can answer: given what 2026 looked like, what should a growing research institution in Taiwan be building in 2027 and beyond?","body_zh":"第一個問題關於運算。一個專案在哪裡不再只是濕實驗生物學，而開始成為模型、管線、資料集或軟體？這一層究竟決定了什麼——它改變了實驗，還是事後補上的裝飾？越來越多得獎團隊的答案是「它改變了實驗」。\n\n第二個問題關於社會。團隊之外有誰接觸過這個專案，而他們改變了什麼？列一串會議紀錄不是整合式人類實踐；因為實驗室外的某個人說了什麼，而讓設計明顯不同，才是。\n\n其餘的部分——趨勢頁、路線圖——都是為了回答第三個只有 GEMS Research 能回答的問題：看過 2026 年的樣貌之後，一個在台灣成長中的研究機構，在 2027 年以後應該建造什麼？"},{"tab":"roadmap","kicker":"Premise","title":"Why the dry lab is the roadmap","title_zh":"為什麼乾實驗室就是路線圖","lede":"GEMS Research is becoming an institution, not a team. Institutions are defined by what they can still do after the current students graduate.","lede_zh":"GEMS Research 正在從一支團隊成為一個機構。機構的定義，在於現在這批學生畢業之後，它還能做什麼。","body":"A wet lab is bounded by its benches, its reagents budget and the hours its students are physically present. A dry lab is bounded by what its people know and what they have written down. That asymmetry is the whole argument: computational capability compounds across years in a way that pipetting skill does not, because a model, a pipeline or a calibrated measurement protocol survives the student who built it.\n\nThis is also where the field has moved. Protein design, metabolic modelling and measurement standardisation are no longer the specialist corner of a project — in 2026 they are frequently the project. The teams on the 2026 podium did not win because they ran more gels.\n\nSo the roadmap below is deliberately about capability, not about any single 2027 project idea. Pick a phase and start.","body_zh":"濕實驗室受限於實驗檯、試劑預算，以及學生實際在場的時數。乾實驗室則受限於人員所知，以及他們寫下了什麼。這個不對稱就是整個論點：運算能力會跨年度累積，而移液技巧不會——因為一個模型、一條管線或一份校正過的量測流程，會比建造它的那位學生留得更久。\n\n這也是整個領域移動的方向。蛋白質設計、代謝建模與量測標準化不再是專案裡的專家角落；在 2026 年，它們經常就是專案本身。站上 2026 頒獎台的團隊，不是因為多跑了幾道膠。\n\n因此以下的路線圖刻意談能力，而不是任何單一的 2027 專案構想。挑一個階段，開始做。"},{"tab":"roadmap","kicker":"The convergence","title":"Two independent analyses, one answer","title_zh":"兩份獨立分析，同一個答案","lede":"The academic trend review and the industry trend review were run separately, from different sources, with no knowledge of each other. They landed on the same white space.","lede_zh":"學術趨勢分析與產業趨勢分析分開進行、來源不同、彼此互不知情。它們指向了同一塊空白地帶。","body":"From the literature side: light has matured from a laboratory curiosity into a real-time actuator for closed-loop control of fermentation, with reported titre gains around 60% in a 1 L photobioreactor — and optogenetics in **Bacillus subtilis** is a twelve-paper literature in the whole of PubMed.\n\nFrom the industry side, reached by an entirely different route: optogenetics is becoming the control and cleaning layer of bioprocessing, because light lets you retrofit an existing steel fermenter instead of building a new one. That makes it the cheapest route past the capital-expenditure wall that is currently the binding constraint on biomanufacturing.\n\nGEMS Research already stands in that gap. ReLEAF was a CcaS/CcaR optogenetic circuit in *Bacillus subtilis* driving a bioreactor, and it won Best Measurement and Best Hardware at high-school level for exactly the instrumentation this line needs. The competition project is over; the research line it opened is not.\n\nThere is a second, blunter finding underneath this. Taiwan's state-backed biotechnology push is a manufacturing play — contract development and manufacturing, GMP capacity — with no visible synthetic-biology **design** layer, while Singapore and Israel are explicitly funding exactly that layer. A small institution cannot out-build a CDMO. It can occupy the design position that nobody in Taiwan currently holds.","body_zh":"從文獻端看：光已經從實驗室的新奇玩意，成熟為可即時操控發酵的閉迴路致動器，1 公升光生物反應器中回報約 60% 的效價提升——而**枯草桿菌（Bacillus subtilis）**的光遺傳學，在整個 PubMed 中只有十二篇文獻。\n\n從產業端看，循著完全不同的路徑：光正在成為生物製程的控制與清潔層，因為光讓你可以改裝既有的不鏽鋼發酵槽，而不必蓋一座新的。這使它成為繞過資本支出高牆最便宜的路徑——而資本支出正是當前生物製造的關鍵瓶頸。\n\nGEMS Research 已經站在這個缺口上。ReLEAF 本來就是在*枯草桿菌*中以 CcaS/CcaR 光遺傳電路驅動生物反應器，並且正是憑著這條路線所需要的儀器化能力，在高中組拿下最佳量測與最佳硬體。競賽專案結束了，它打開的研究路線沒有。\n\n底下還有第二個更直白的發現。台灣由國家支持的生技推動是製造導向的——委託開發製造、GMP 產能——看不到合成生物學的**設計**層；而新加坡與以色列正明確地投資的，正是這一層。一個小型機構無法在產能上贏過 CDMO，但它可以佔住台灣目前沒有人佔住的設計位置。"},{"id":"good-patterns","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What separated real engagement from outreach theatre","title_zh":"真正的參與，和表演式推廣，差別在哪裡","lede":"Across the 2026 field, the teams whose Science for Good work counted did four things the rest did not.","lede_zh":"綜觀 2026 年的參賽團隊，那些「科學向善」真正有份量的隊伍，做了另外四件其他人沒做的事。","body":"**They designed education from data, then measured it like an experiment.** UCAS-China did not start from \"raise awareness\". It ran clinician interviews and a 461-person questionnaire, found that patients stop medication once they feel better and that parents refuse to start it for children out of fear of side effects, and made *compliance* the target instead of awareness. UOregon wrote three separate curricula for three audiences with different prior knowledge and ran them as three DBTL iterations across June, July and October, carrying each round's lessons forward. HFI ran everything through a five-step cycle it named CLEAR, in which **every activity had to report a measured outcome and a change for the next iteration**.\n\nThe sharpest version of this is publishing the results when they are bad. GEMS-Taiwan ran pre- and post-lesson surveys with 140 students across five schools and published per-question accuracy charts including the failures — only 30% of students got DNA base pairing right. That number is worth more to the next teacher than any photograph of a full classroom.\n\n**They trained themselves before training anybody else.** Nineteen GU Frankfurt members took the \"Basics of Science Communication\" workshop run by NaWik, Germany's national institute for science communication, and used its core-message and cloverleaf tools as the basis of everything that followed. Most teams treat communication as something you already know how to do because you can talk.\n\n**They put disagreeing people in the same room.** Oxford's *Buzz In* podcast is the most quietly radical format in the 2026 field: rather than interviewing stakeholders separately and summarising, it deliberately paired people who disagree — a Varroa-resistance academic with a commercial beekeeper on whether to treat at all, then an industry council CEO with amateur beekeepers. Disagreement is the thing most human-practices pages are built to smooth over; Oxford made it the content.\n\nKIT won Inclusivity by turning the same honesty inward. It read the iGEM Diversity and Inclusion Committee's own writing, surveyed five previous iGEM gender-equity projects, and noticed that nearly all of them face **outward** — role models, outreach to girls, awareness — and almost none examine the team itself. So KIT examined the team itself.\n\n**They quantified the need, and built a business model that was not \"sell the product\".** Oxford states the problem in numbers rather than adjectives: Australia's failed Varroa eradication cost A$101 million and destroyed about 30,000 hives; surveyed US commercial operations lost roughly 62% of colonies in 2024–25. DTU-Denmark anchors on a date and a measurement: the Danish wind industry's voluntary landfill ban took effect on 1 January 2026, and a Danish EPA screening detected bisphenol A in every tank leaching test on blade material.\n\nThen the models themselves. HongKong-JSS sells **Certification-as-a-Service** — farmers subscribe annually, the team tests soil on site, passing farms get a \"Heavy Metal-Free\" logo for supermarket packaging that earns a premium, and surprise re-tests throughout the year are affordable precisely because the test is cheap. GEMS-Taiwan deploys through farmer collectives rather than direct sales, because its own fleet analysis shows a reactor owned by a single farm sits idle most of the season. GU Frankfurt chose exclusive licensing over a start-up because an autologous cell therapy's facility and specialist-salary costs cannot be carried by a spin-out, and has a letter of support from Miltenyi Biotec to show for it. XJTLU-China gives catmaOS away, on the argument that accessibility *is* the commercial thesis.\n\nUAlberta's case is the most evidentially careful: demand is tabulated by customer role **with the strength of each piece of evidence named** — two clinician letters of support, a signed letter of intent from one clinic, 86% of 38 surveyed dry eye patients interested, an application at interview stage with Nucleate Canada. And UCAS-China opens its commercial section by stating outright that the case must rest on a defined unmet need rather than on technological novelty, then tabulates the strengths of the existing drugs it would have to displace. A team willing to argue against itself is a team worth believing.","body_zh":"**他們從資料出發設計教育，再像做實驗一樣去量測它。** UCAS-China 的起點不是「提升認知」。他們訪談臨床醫師、做了 461 人的問卷，發現病人一感覺好轉就停藥、家長因為害怕副作用而不願意讓孩子開始用藥，於是把目標從「認知」改成*服藥遵從性*。UOregon 為三種先備知識不同的對象寫了三套獨立課程，並在六月、七月與十月以三次 DBTL 迭代執行，把每一輪的教訓帶進下一輪。HFI 則讓所有活動都跑一個他們命名為 CLEAR 的五步驟循環，其中**每一項活動都必須回報一個量測到的結果，以及下一次要改什麼**。\n\n這件事最鋒利的版本，是在結果難看的時候照樣公布。GEMS-Taiwan 在五所學校對 140 名學生做了課前課後問卷，並公布逐題正確率圖表，包含失敗的部分——DNA 鹼基配對只有 30% 的學生答對。對下一位老師而言，這個數字比任何一張坐滿學生的照片都有價值。\n\n**他們先訓練自己，再去訓練別人。** GU Frankfurt 有 19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息與四葉草等工具作為後續一切的基礎。多數團隊把傳播當成「反正我會說話就會做」的事。\n\n**他們把意見不合的人放進同一個房間。** Oxford 的 *Buzz In* podcast 是 2026 年最安靜地激進的形式：它不是分別訪談各方再做摘要，而是刻意把意見相左的人配成一對——讓研究 Varroa 抗性的學者與商業養蜂人辯論「到底該不該用藥」，再讓產業公會執行長與業餘養蜂人對談。多數人類實踐頁面的設計目的就是把分歧抹平；Oxford 直接把分歧當成內容。\n\nKIT 則把同樣的誠實轉向內部，因而拿下包容性獎。他們讀了 iGEM 多元與包容委員會自己的文章，檢視了五個過去的 iGEM 性別平等專案，注意到它們幾乎全部朝**外**——榜樣、對女孩的推廣、意識提升——而幾乎沒有一個檢視團隊自身。於是 KIT 檢視了團隊自身。\n\n**他們把需求量化，而且做出來的商業模式不是「把產品賣掉」。** Oxford 用數字而非形容詞陳述問題：澳洲失敗的 Varroa 根除行動花了 1.01 億澳元、摧毀約 3 萬個蜂箱；受調查的美國商業蜂場在 2024–25 年損失了約 62% 的蜂群。DTU-Denmark 則錨定在一個日期與一次量測上：丹麥風電產業的自願掩埋禁令自 2026 年 1 月 1 日生效，而丹麥環保署的篩檢在葉片材料的每一次槽式溶出試驗中都測到雙酚 A。\n\n接著是商業模式本身。HongKong-JSS 賣的是**認證即服務**——農民年度訂閱，團隊到場檢測土壤，通過的農場取得「無重金屬」標章可用於超市包裝並賣出溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢之所以負擔得起，正是因為檢測又便宜又快。GEMS-Taiwan 透過農民合作社而非直接銷售來部署，因為他們自己的機隊分析顯示：單一農場自有的反應器一整季大部分時間都閒置。GU Frankfurt 選擇獨家授權而非自行創業，因為自體細胞治療的廠房與專業人力成本不是一間新創扛得起的，而他們手上有 Miltenyi Biotec 的支持信。XJTLU-China 則把 catmaOS 免費釋出，理由是可及性*本身*就是商業論點。\n\nUAlberta 的案例在證據上最為嚴謹：需求依客戶角色列表，而且**每一項證據的強度都被標明**——兩封臨床醫師支持信、一間診所簽署的意向書、38 位乾眼症受訪患者中 86% 有興趣、一件已進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 申請。UCAS-China 則在商業章節的開頭直接寫明：這個案子必須建立在明確的未滿足需求上，而不是技術新穎性，接著列表說明它必須取代的既有藥物有哪些優點。一支願意對自己提出反方論證的團隊，才值得相信。","cards":[{"kicker":"The format worth stealing","title":"Oxford's Buzz In: put the disagreement on the record","title_zh":"Oxford 的 Buzz In：把分歧記錄下來","body":"A three-episode podcast that deliberately paired stakeholders who disagree, rather than interviewing them separately and summarising. Episode one put a Varroa-resistance academic opposite a commercial beekeeper on whether to treat at all. Most human-practices pages exist to smooth disagreement away; this one makes it the content, and it is far harder to fake than a list of meetings.","body_zh":"一個三集的 podcast，刻意把意見相左的利害關係人配對，而不是分別訪談後再做摘要。第一集讓研究 Varroa 抗性的學者，與商業養蜂人正面交鋒「到底該不該用藥」。多數人類實踐頁面的存在目的是把分歧抹平；這一個把分歧變成內容，而且它比一份會議清單難假造得多。","chips":["3 episodes","paired opponents"]},{"kicker":"The habit worth stealing","title":"Publish the question your students got wrong","title_zh":"公布學生答錯的那一題","body":"GEMS-Taiwan surveyed 140 students across five schools before and after each lesson and published per-question accuracy — including DNA base pairing, where only 30% answered correctly. Reporting the failure makes the whole dataset credible and hands the next teacher something actionable. A photograph of a full classroom does neither.","body_zh":"GEMS-Taiwan 在五所學校對 140 名學生做課前課後問卷，並公布逐題正確率——包括 DNA 鹼基配對，只有 30% 答對。報告失敗讓整份資料變得可信，也交給下一位老師一個可以採取行動的東西。一張坐滿學生的照片兩者都做不到。","chips":["140 students · 5 schools","30% on base pairing"]},{"kicker":"The habit worth stealing","title":"Train the team before training the public","title_zh":"先訓練團隊，再去教公眾","body":"Nineteen GU Frankfurt members took the Basics of Science Communication workshop from NaWik, Germany's national science-communication institute, and built everything afterwards on its core-message and cloverleaf tools. Science communication is a craft with a literature; almost every other team treats it as something you can already do because you can talk.","body_zh":"GU Frankfurt 有 19 位成員上了德國國家科學傳播研究所 NaWik 的「科學傳播基礎」工作坊，並以其核心訊息與四葉草工具為基礎建構後續所有內容。科學傳播是一門有文獻的技藝；幾乎其他所有團隊都把它當成「我會說話所以我就會」。","chips":["19 members trained","NaWik"]},{"kicker":"The business model worth stealing","title":"Sell the certificate, not the instrument","title_zh":"賣證書，不要賣儀器","body":"HongKong-JSS does not sell its mercury assay. Farmers subscribe annually, the team tests on site, passing farms get a 'Heavy Metal-Free' logo for supermarket packaging that commands a premium, and surprise re-tests through the year keep the certificate honest — affordable precisely because the test itself is cheap. The cheapness of the science becomes the business model rather than a weakness.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 不賣他們的汞檢測。農民年度訂閱，團隊到場檢測，通過的農場取得可用於超市包裝的「無重金屬」標章並賣出溢價，而全年不定期的突擊複檢維持證書的公信力——之所以負擔得起，正因為檢測本身很便宜。科學的廉價在這裡變成商業模式，而不是弱點。","chips":["Certification-as-a-Service","surprise re-tests"]},{"kicker":"The business model worth stealing","title":"Name the strength of each piece of evidence","title_zh":"標明每一項證據的強度","body":"UAlberta tabulates demand by customer role and says how strong each item is: two clinician letters of support, one signed letter of intent, 86% of 38 surveyed patients interested, one application at interview stage with Nucleate Canada. A letter of intent and a survey response are not the same kind of evidence, and saying so is what makes the table worth reading.","body_zh":"UAlberta 依客戶角色把需求列表，並說明每一項證據有多強：兩封臨床醫師支持信、一封已簽署的意向書、38 位受訪患者中 86% 有興趣、一件進入面試階段的 Nucleate Canada 申請。一封意向書和一份問卷回覆不是同一種證據，而把這件事講清楚，正是這張表值得讀的原因。","chips":["evidence graded by strength"]},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"Argue against yourself in public","title_zh":"公開地為自己提出反方論證","body":"UCAS-China opens its commercial section by saying the case must rest on unmet need rather than technological novelty, then lists what the existing drugs do well. GEMS-Taiwan publishes a 68-year payback against a partner's 4.9-year figure and names the disagreement instead of resolving it. This is the practice that most distinguishes the 2026 podium, and it costs nothing but nerve.","body_zh":"UCAS-China 在商業章節的開頭就說：這個案子必須建立在未滿足需求上，而非技術新穎性，接著列出既有藥物的優點。GEMS-Taiwan 公布了 68 年的回收期，對照合作夥伴算出的 4.9 年，並指名這個歧異而不去解決它。這是 2026 年頒獎台上最顯著的共同做法，而它唯一的代價是膽識。","chips":["no budget required"]}],"method":"Drawn from the Science for Good fields of the team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Audience numbers and survey sizes are the teams' own figures and are not independently verified. The judgement about what 'counted' is ours; the team files and the wikis behind them are linked so a reader can disagree. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and appears here on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料取自本報告團隊檔案中的「科學向善」欄位，每一份都來自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。參與人數與問卷樣本數為各隊自報數字，未經獨立查證。關於「什麼才算數」的判斷出自我們；團隊檔案與其背後的 wiki 都附有連結，讀者可以自行判斷是否同意。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，在此與其他隊伍適用相同標準。"},{"id":"highschool-ceiling","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"The high-school ceiling, measured honestly","title_zh":"誠實地量一次高中組的天花板","lede":"What a high-school dry lab can actually reach in one season — and the finding that the gap is not about tools.","lede_zh":"一個高中乾實驗室在一季之內真正能做到什麼——以及那個發現：差距不在工具。","body":"Read the ten High School Top 10 dry labs side by side and the first surprise is how ordinary the software is. **Eton-College-UK** built its protease substrate predictor out of L2-regularised logistic regression and a BLOSUM62-smoothed position-specific scoring matrix — techniques older than the students using them. **HFI** used NetLogo, which is free and was designed for schools. **GHCIS** used a local install of NUPACK. **HangzhouFourteenAP** used PyMOL and FoldX. **HKSSC** used AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera and HotSpot Wizard. **HongKong-HS** reused another team's tool outright — miRADAR, released by Wageningen's 2024 team — rather than rebuilding it. Almost none of this costs money, and none of it requires a cluster.\n\nOnly **Lambert-GA**, the Grand Prize winner, works at the frontier of the toolchain: BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic. And even there the thing that earned Best Model was not the tools. It was that they **benchmarked the confidence metrics themselves** — ipSAE, ipTM and a 38-metric ensemble, against 5,721 labelled experimental designs — found the ensemble barely beat chance at ROC-AUC 0.541, noticed that their own eventual hit did not have the best score, and published all of that rather than quietly reporting the hit.\n\nThat is the pattern, and it holds across the whole tier. **The differentiator at high-school level is evaluation discipline, not tool sophistication.**\n\nThe evidence is specific. Eton clustered near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, then ran a label-shuffle control and a composition-only ablation — three cheap steps that separate a real classifier from a leaky one. **HongKong-JSS** split runs into calibration and validation *before* fitting anything, subtracted a matched control from the same run and timepoint, and reported RMSE on held-out runs with the failures left in. HKSSC could not measure molar enzyme concentration, so rather than report an invalid *k*cat/*K*m they defined and justified a mass-normalised metric valid only below *K*m, then ran a two-way ANOVA, found unequal variances, and moved to a median-based test. GHCIS specified its colour-classification algorithm down to the equation and the threshold, including an explicit **\"unresolved, and must not be read as Negative\"** state, and shipped it with one-command Docker deployment. HangzhouFourteenAP reported the prediction that lost: FoldX ranked Y166Q first, the bench preferred Q172P, and the wiki revises its own ranking while using BCA normalisation to rule out protein load as the explanation.\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan** belongs on that list and is worth reading closely, because the wiki is unusually candid about its own weaknesses. The strengths are real: a genuinely pre-registered growth-rate forecast, registered on 1 October and scored on run 6, which landed inside its stated interval; an autoencoder that flagged a failing photometer 26.7 hours before it died; and a crop-stress index fitted to 25 years of county rice yields rather than to expert judgement. The weaknesses are stated by the team itself: secreted activity at n=1 and below the limit of quantitation; two induction runs that disagree on the *sign* of the change; a Hill curve assumed to hold at 20 L when every induction ran at a single light intensity; a 2.44× rice canopy correction that is modelled, not measured; an efficacy coefficient of 0.58 explicitly withdrawn; and a payback period of 68 years on the team's own loss figure against a partner's 4.9 years, with the disagreement named rather than resolved. Naming the disagreement instead of picking the flattering number is the practice worth keeping.\n\n**And the control case.** **GCGS** reached the High School Top 10 with no model page and no software page at all — both routes return 404. Its one modelling claim is an undocumented circuit-level simulation with no parameters, equations or tooling named. A team can still place in the top ten of its section with essentially no dry lab. What GCGS could not do is win a modelling, measurement or software prize, and that is the precise shape of the opportunity.","body_zh":"把高中組 Top 10 的十個乾實驗室並排來讀，第一個意外是：他們用的軟體有多麼普通。**Eton-College-UK** 的蛋白酶受質預測器，是用 L2 正規化的 logistic regression 加上以 BLOSUM62 平滑的位置特異性計分矩陣（PSSM）做出來的——這些技術比使用它們的學生還老。**HFI** 用的是 NetLogo，免費，而且本來就是為學校設計的。**GHCIS** 用本機安裝的 NUPACK。**HangzhouFourteenAP** 用 PyMOL 與 FoldX。**HKSSC** 用 AlphaFold、UCSF Chimera 與 HotSpot Wizard。**HongKong-HS** 則直接沿用別隊的工具——Wageningen 2024 年釋出的 miRADAR——而不是重做一個。這些幾乎都不花錢，也都不需要叢集運算。\n\n只有總冠軍 **Lambert-GA** 站在工具鏈的前沿：BindCraft、Boltz-2、Protenix、Mosaic。但即使在那裡，替他們贏得最佳模型的也不是工具，而是他們**對信心指標本身做了基準測試**——拿 ipSAE、ipTM 與一組 38 項指標的集成，去對照 5,721 個有實驗標註的設計——發現該集成的 ROC-AUC 只有 0.541，幾乎只比亂猜好一點，還注意到自己最後成功的那個設計分數並不是最高的，然後把這一切全部公開，而不是安靜地只報成功的那一個。\n\n這就是整個型態，而且在整個層級中都成立。**高中層級的差異來自評估的紀律，而不是工具的精密度。**\n\n證據很具體。Eton 以 Hamming 距離把近似重複的序列分群，再把整群一起分到同一個 fold，接著跑標籤洗牌對照與僅用胺基酸組成的消融測試——三個便宜的步驟，就把一個真正的分類器和一個資料外洩的分類器分開了。**HongKong-JSS** 在擬合任何東西*之前*就把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組，扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對照，並在保留批次上報告 RMSE，而且把失敗的資料留在裡面。HKSSC 無法量到酵素的莫耳濃度，於是沒有去報一個無效的 *k*cat/*K*m，而是定義並論證了一個只在低於 *K*m 時有效的質量標準化指標，接著做雙因子 ANOVA，發現變異數不齊，再改用以中位數為基礎的檢定。GHCIS 把顏色判讀演算法寫到方程式與閾值的層級，包含一個明確的**「無法判定，且不得視為陰性」**狀態，並以一行指令的 Docker 部署出貨。HangzhouFourteenAP 報告了那個輸掉的預測：FoldX 把 Y166Q 排第一，實驗卻偏好 Q172P，而 wiki 修正了自己的排序，同時用 BCA 標準化排除「蛋白質上樣量不同」這個解釋。\n\n**GEMS-Taiwan** 也屬於這份名單，而且值得仔細讀，因為這個 wiki 對自身弱點的坦白程度相當罕見。強項是真的：一個貨真價實的預先登記成長率預測，10 月 1 日登記、在第 6 批次評分，結果落在所宣告的區間內；一個在光度計故障前 26.7 小時就示警的自編碼器；以及一個以 25 年各縣市稻作產量擬合、而非靠專家判斷加權的作物逆境指數。弱點則由團隊自己寫出來：分泌活性 n=1 且低於定量極限；兩次誘導實驗對變化的*正負號*彼此矛盾；Hill 曲線被假定在 20 公升仍然成立，但所有誘導都只在單一光強度下進行；2.44 倍的水稻冠層修正是模擬出來而非量出來的；一個 0.58 的效能係數被明確撤回；以及以團隊自己的損失數字計算出 68 年的回收期，對比合作夥伴算出的 4.9 年，而這個歧異被指名寫出，而不是被解決掉。把歧異寫出來、而不是挑一個好看的數字，正是值得保留的做法。\n\n**還有對照組。** **GCGS** 在完全沒有 model 頁也沒有 software 頁的情況下進入高中組 Top 10——兩個路徑都回傳 404。它唯一的建模主張，是一個沒有記載參數、方程式或工具名稱的電路層級模擬。一支隊伍確實可以幾乎沒有乾實驗室，仍然進入該組前十名。但 GCGS 做不到的是拿下建模、測量或軟體獎項——而那正是機會的確切形狀。","cards":[{"kicker":"The ceiling","title":"Lambert-GA, and what the frontier costs","title_zh":"Lambert-GA，以及站上前沿的代價","body":"Four linked models: protein-design metric benchmarking on 5,721 labelled designs, a Sobol-analysed oral pharmacokinetic model, a 13-ODE SimBiology RNAi network, and an individual-based six-year, 800-run colony epidemiology. They produced the first reported DWV VP3 minibinder for under $400 of compute, released the open-source PRINCE site ranker (45.8% top-3 hit rate against 23.8% random on a no-homolog subset), and an $80 dryer externally validated at two universities. This is the ceiling, and it is reachable.","body_zh":"四個彼此連動的模型：在 5,721 個有標註的設計上做蛋白質設計指標的基準測試、一個經 Sobol 分析的口服藥物動力學模型、一個 13 條 ODE 的 SimBiology RNAi 網路，以及一個為期六年、跑 800 次的個體導向族群流行病學模擬。他們以不到 400 美元的運算成本做出第一個被報導的 DWV VP3 minibinder，釋出開源的 PRINCE 位點排序工具（在無同源子集上，前三名命中率 45.8%，對照隨機的 23.8%），以及一台 80 美元、經兩所大學外部驗證的乾燥裝置。這就是天花板，而且搆得到。","chips":["Boltz-2 · BindCraft · Protenix","under $400 of compute"]},{"kicker":"The floor","title":"GCGS: Top 10 with no dry lab at all","title_zh":"GCGS：完全沒有乾實驗室也能進 Top 10","body":"Both /model and /software return 404. The single modelling claim is an undocumented circuit-level simulation with no parameters, equations or tooling named. GCGS still reached the High School Top 10 on the strength of a clean two-cycle DBTL and its Best New Improved Part. Read it as the honest floor: the dry lab is not what gets you into the top ten — it is what gets you a prize.","body_zh":"/model 與 /software 都回傳 404。唯一的建模主張是一個沒有記載參數、方程式或工具名稱的電路層級模擬。GCGS 仍然憑著乾淨的兩輪 DBTL 與最佳改良基因元件獎進入高中組 Top 10。請把它讀成誠實的底線：乾實驗室不是讓你擠進前十名的東西——它是讓你拿到獎項的東西。","chips":["no model page","still Top 10"]},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Three cheap controls that separate real from leaky","title_zh":"三個便宜的對照，分開真實與外洩","body":"From Eton-College-UK, and transferable to any student machine-learning project: cluster near-duplicate sequences by Hamming distance and split whole clusters across folds, so the model cannot memorise a near-copy; run a label-shuffle control, which must collapse to chance; run an ablation that strips the information you claim to be using. None of these needs a GPU. Together they turn a high-school classifier into something a reviewer can believe.","body_zh":"來自 Eton-College-UK，可移植到任何學生的機器學習專案：以 Hamming 距離把近似重複的序列分群，並把整群分到同一個 fold，讓模型無法記住近似副本；跑標籤洗牌對照，其表現必須塌回隨機水準；跑一個消融測試，剝除你宣稱正在使用的那項資訊。這些都不需要 GPU。合起來，它們能把一個高中生的分類器變成審閱者願意相信的東西。","chips":["cluster-aware CV","label shuffle","ablation"]},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Split before you fit","title_zh":"先切分，再擬合","body":"HongKong-JSS divided its runs into calibration and validation before fitting anything, subtracted a matched control from the same run and timepoint, inverted the fit to predict unknowns, and reported RMSE on the held-out runs with the failures left in — then published a list of the statistics they had not yet done. That last habit is rarer and more valuable than the first.","body_zh":"HongKong-JSS 在擬合任何東西之前就把實驗批次分成校正組與驗證組，扣除同一批次、同一時間點的對照，反解擬合式來預測未知樣本，並在保留批次上報告 RMSE、把失敗的資料留在裡面——接著公布了一份他們還沒做的統計分析清單。最後這個習慣比第一個更罕見，也更有價值。","chips":["held-out RMSE","published what is not yet done"]},{"kicker":"The pattern","title":"Publish the prediction that lost","title_zh":"公開那個輸掉的預測","body":"HangzhouFourteenAP's FoldX pipeline ranked Y166Q first; the bench preferred Q172P. Rather than bury it, the wiki revises its own ranking, demotes the failed candidate to a mechanistic probe, and uses BCA normalisation to rule out protein load as the confound. Lambert-GA did the same at a larger scale by showing its own hit was not the top-scoring design. A dry lab earns more credibility from one well-controlled loss than from three unexamined wins.","body_zh":"HangzhouFourteenAP 的 FoldX 流程把 Y166Q 排第一，實驗卻偏好 Q172P。他們沒有把它埋掉，而是在 wiki 上修正自己的排序，把失敗的候選降級為機制探針，並以 BCA 標準化排除「蛋白質上樣量」這個干擾因子。Lambert-GA 在更大的尺度上做了同樣的事：證明自己成功的那個設計並不是分數最高的。一個乾實驗室從一次控制良好的失敗中得到的可信度，大於三次未經檢驗的成功。","chips":["FoldX said Y166Q","the bench said Q172P"]},{"kicker":"For GEMS","title":"The gap is one term of teaching, not a budget line","title_zh":"差距是一個學期的教學，不是一筆預算","body":"Every practice above — cluster-aware splits, label-shuffle controls, calibration/validation separation, provenance tagging, publishing the loss — costs nothing but attention and can be taught in a term. The tools the 2026 high-school field actually used are free: NetLogo, NUPACK, PyMOL, FoldX, scikit-learn, ImageJ, Chimera, the AlphaFold server. GEMS does not need to buy its way to the ceiling. It needs to make evaluation discipline the house style.","body_zh":"上述每一項做法——分群感知的資料切分、標籤洗牌對照、校正與驗證分離、來源標註、公開失敗——都不花錢，只花注意力，而且一個學期就能教完。2026 年高中組實際用到的工具都是免費的：NetLogo、NUPACK、PyMOL、FoldX、scikit-learn、ImageJ、Chimera、AlphaFold server。GEMS 不需要靠花錢爬上天花板，它需要的是把評估紀律變成自己的風格。","chips":["all free tools","one term"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Headline dry-lab work","Main tools","The discipline that stands out"],"head_zh":["團隊","乾實驗室重點工作","主要工具","最突出的紀律"],"rows":[["Lambert-GA","Four linked models: de novo minibinder design, oral PK, 13-ODE RNAi network, colony epidemiology","BindCraft, Boltz-2, Protenix, Mosaic","Benchmarked the confidence metrics themselves and published that its own hit was not top-scoring"],["Eton-College-UK","Seven-protease substrate predictor on 10,472 cleavage windows","scikit-learn, PSSM, BLOSUM62, VHSE","Hamming-cluster-aware cross-validation, label-shuffle and ablation controls"],["GEMS-Taiwan","Crop-stress index fitted to 25 years of county rice yields; optogenetic circuit; anomaly detection","Python, autoencoder, Kalman filter, ERA5, QGIS, AlphaFold","A pre-registered forecast scored after the fact, and a published disagreement between its own runs"],["GHCIS","Toehold design pipeline, plus ARGUS, a deployable colour-classification platform","NUPACK 4.1.0.1, Node.js, Docker, SQLite","Algorithm specified to the threshold, with an explicit 'unresolved' state"],["HongKong-JSS","Calibration and inverse prediction for an in-field mercury assay","ImageJ, log-linear calibration, Onshape, ESP32","Calibration/validation split before fitting; RMSE on held-out runs with failures left in"],["HKSSC","Structure-guided mutagenesis and enzyme kinetics for a paraben-degrading esterase","AlphaFold, UCSF Chimera, HotSpot Wizard, CB-Dock2","Invented a justified mass-normalised metric rather than report an invalid kcat/Km"],["HFI","Agent-based contact model and a 13-variable ODE system, both as wet-lab gatekeepers","NetLogo 3D, Runge-Kutta, interactive HTML front-ends","Screened seven RBS parts computationally before a single plasmid was built"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","Mutation prioritisation pipeline for CoGH66","PyMOL, FoldX, MAFFT, AlphaFold Server","Reported the computational prediction the bench overturned, with the confound controlled"],["HongKong-HS","Toehold switch thermodynamics for a urinary miRNA screening kit","NUPACK, miRADAR (Wageningen iGEM 2024)","Reused another team's released tool instead of rebuilding it"],["GCGS","No model or software page exists","—","The control case: Top 10 without a dry lab, but no modelling prize"]]},"method":"Drawn from the ten High School Top 10 team files in this report, each researched from the team's own 2026 wiki. Tool lists are what each team names; a team may have used more than it wrote down. The judgement about what 'stands out' is ours, and a reader who disagrees should open the team file and the wiki behind it — both are linked. GEMS-Taiwan is the report author's own team and has been assessed on the same terms as the rest.","method_zh":"資料來自本報告中高中組 Top 10 的十份團隊檔案，每一份都取自該隊自己的 2026 wiki。工具清單是各隊自己寫出來的；團隊實際用到的可能多於其所記載。關於「什麼最突出」的判斷出自我們，不同意的讀者可以直接打開團隊檔案與其背後的 wiki——兩者都有連結。GEMS-Taiwan 是本報告作者自己的團隊，評判標準與其他隊伍相同。"},{"id":"ihp-depth","tab":"good","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"Who actually let the outside world change the science","lede":"Across 93 teams, closing the loop has stopped being the distinction and become the norm — and almost every loop that closed was closed by a credentialled expert rather than by anybody the criterion is rhetorically about.","body":"A score of four is a sentence, not a stakeholder list: a name, a specific thing said, and a design that is visibly different afterwards. Wageningen's Triton has three modules rather than one because Peter Fischer of Aqualab Zuid explained that trifluoroacetate can only be measured by LC-MS at a central lab, which forced an on-site biosensor, and because Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian showed that even tenfold reverse-osmosis concentration leaves it far too dilute, which forced a capture module. **GEMS-Taiwan** was releasing engineered Bacillus into soil until Prof. Chen Wen-Liang told them it could be neither contained nor made to sense temperature precisely; the hollow-fibre perfusion reactor and the electronic AIoT sensing layer both came out of that one April conversation. UCAS-China dropped NKX2-1 as a cargo and put SLPI in its place because Professor Huaiyong Chen said the first matters in development and barely in adulthood. RDFZ-China built bcsABCD in both BL21(DE3) and C41(DE3) and switched host after Professor Haibo Zhang warned that a working genetic module does not imply an efficient one; WUXI-DSAS excised gtdT on Dr Tengfei Hu's advice and recovered the linear dose-response its first-generation sensor could not give; IISER-Kolkata rebuilt its kill-switch trigger around the hypochlorite-sensing regulator RclR after a wastewater engineer pointed out that Indian plants disinfect with sodium hypochlorite rather than UV; and Oxford gave up a living Snodgrassella symbiont for heat-inactivated yeast because regulators pushed back against the beekeepers who had asked for it, then published what that cost its own users.\n\nThe three Best IHP winners share a method, and it is organisational rather than intellectual: the practice is wired into the engineering, not appended to it. **TU Delft** ran Value Sensitive Design in three declared passes and translated values into requirements, labelling the ones it could not meet as Future Perspectives rather than dropping them quietly; UCAS-China built its RCSF cycle as a deliberate parallel to DBTL and gave the human practices group the standing job of tracking every subteam's bottleneck; GEMS-Taiwan ran four thematic expert pipelines with five continuously engaged experts. What the winners do not have is a monopoly on depth. Oxford, Wageningen and UFABC-Brazil were nominees with chains at least as traceable, and UFABC declared its confirmation and refutation rules before seeing its survey results, then redrew its own SWOT when two assumptions failed. **Madrid-UCM**, which published the only genuine closure criterion in the cohort, got no human practices nomination at all.\n\nThe formats that changed designs are narrow and unglamorous. One of them is a single conversation with whoever operates the thing: Veolia's technical director for LYON, a sulfur-recovery engineer of thirty-three years for UOttawa, an optometrist for UAlberta, wet-market vendors for HongKong-JSS who demanded a number and got a wavelength-resolved spectrometer in place of a 14-channel colour sensor. Another is protocol-level consultation with whoever actually runs the technique, which is where chassis and construct changes come from: DTU to Komagataella phaffii, NFLSHS-CHINA from two plasmids to one, Heidelberg to a Serratia expression cassette. Add regulators contacted while the design is still open, peer teams handing over negative data as Darmstadt 2025 did to Padua on pcrABCD's oxygen sensitivity, and written-scorecard pitch events, which are cheap and work: Stanford's BIOME Shark Tank produced the microneedle segmentation pipeline. Against that, the school workshop, the museum stand, the carnival booth, the panel discussion and SDG mapping produced headcounts and nothing traceable, and the large public survey changed vocabulary with near-perfect reliability and hardware almost never.\n\nThe high-school tier is fully competitive wherever the work is user-facing and iterative. HongKong-JSS's farm-driven hardware revisions, measured as a drop from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent coefficient of variation, are better user-led engineering than most collegiate teams managed; **Hongwen School** struck three marketing claims on a gastroenterologist's evidence ladder and changed its selection antibiotic on a professor's re-annotation; HFI, NFLSHS-CHINA, RDFZ-China and WUXI-DSAS all changed circuits or hosts for a named reason; and QingdaoAcademy compressed twenty-two activities into thirteen numbered decisions that split a one-pot process in two and abandoned a planned pH-based function switch outright. Where the tier is not competitive is institutional reach: nothing in it approaches Oxford's EPA-FDA-USDA-CBD mapping, Wageningen's analysis of the non-viable-GMO approval route, UCL's Water UK discharge gap or DTU's correspondence with the European Environment Agency, and formal ethics infrastructure is rare, with Baltimore's community-lab board the main exception; the tier also almost never publishes failures of access the way DTU names the turbine makers who never replied.\n\nThe uncomfortable finding is who actually caused the changes. Of 64 teams that closed a loop, the loop was closed by a credentialled technical expert in nearly every case; the publics, patients and communities that the criterion is rhetorically about overwhelmingly changed the vocabulary and not the vector. Cornell's burn survivors changed what the team promises, Princeton's myeloma patients changed the word 'virus', HFI's 434 respondents changed 'genetically modified' to 'engineered' — all real, none of it touching a construct. Genuine counter-examples number six or seven in 93: LYON removed every living cell from its filter because the public objected, ICJFLS turned public fear into a four-layer containment design, HongKong-JSS re-specified a sensor because farmers wanted a number, UFABC-Brazil routed its seizure alert to a caregiver because a psychiatrist in the public system pointed out that patients who cannot recognise an aura cannot act on one, a beauty-salon manager's distrust of local seaweed put ultrafiltration desalting and endotoxin limits into QingdaoAcademy's plan, and a landfill worker of six years gave Hongwen School the handling cost that made local processing a hard constraint. Two further discomforts: the branded cycle acronym is now universal and predicts nothing, with Jilin-China's Social Shaping Loop and GreatBay-SCIE's five-stage framework scoring 2 while plain tables score 4; and awards track legibility rather than consequence, since **KIT** won Inclusivity and GreatBay-SCIE was nominated for Best IHP on evidence that scores 2, while Madrid-UCM, Hongwen School, GYHS and WUXI-DSAS closed loops nobody rewarded.","cards":[{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"Two of three modules were somebody else's idea","body":"Wageningen set out only to degrade trifluoroacetate. Peter Fischer at Aqualab Zuid, one of six labs legally tasked with assessing Dutch drinking water, explained that the compound can only be measured by LC-MS on samples shipped to a central lab, so the bioreactor could not be operated at all without an on-site readout: that created the biosensor module. Bert van der Waal and Peyman Salehian then showed that tenfold reverse-osmosis concentration takes 2.2 micrograms per litre only to 22, against a milligram-per-litre target, which created the capture module. Frank Schoonenberg of Vitens moved the whole deployment target to reverse-osmosis concentrate, and Tue Kjaergaard Nielsen changed the readout to released fluoride because measuring TFA disappearance mistakes adsorption for degradation.","chips":["WageningenUR","Overgrad","Score 4","Utility and lab engineers"]},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"The conversation that moved sensing out of the cell","body":"GEMS-Taiwan's original design put engineered Bacillus subtilis in the soil with a DesK-DesR system reading temperature directly. On 10 April, Prof. Chen Wen-Liang and bioprocess experts said two things were wrong: the bacteria could not be contained, and biological sensing was neither precise nor controllable enough. Sensing moved out of the cell into electronic sensors and an AIoT model, and a hollow-fibre perfusion bioreactor was built to hold the bacteria in while letting the protectants out. A later public forum with natural-farming advocates, who argued that a crop protected from every stress never builds tolerance, became the specification for the release threshold rather than an objection to be managed.","chips":["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","Score 4","Best IHP winner"]},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"When the regulator overrules the user","body":"Danny Le Feuvre of the Australian Honey Bee Industry Council and Mike Allerton of Amateur Beekeepers Australia both wanted a persistent living Snodgrassella alvi gut symbiont because it minimises beekeeper labour. Oxford did not simply comply: it took the question to Scottish and Australian regulators and the Soil Association, who pushed the other way, and switched to heat-inactivated dried yeast. The team then stated plainly what that cost — the persistence the beekeepers valued, meaning repeat dosing and more labour. A joint meeting with EPA, FDA and USDA staff stopped them treating the inactivated route as a universal regulatory shortcut, forcing jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction mapping instead.","chips":["Oxford","Undergrad","Score 4","Best IHP nominee"]},{"kicker":"Worked example","title":"A farmer asked for a number","body":"HongKong-JSS built a mercury biosensor with a visible colour readout. Koo's Farm and local wet-market vendors said they wanted numerical readings, not qualitative colour, which is the direct reason the AS7343 14-channel sensor was replaced by a wavelength-resolved Hamamatsu C12880 with a numerical display. Users then reported excessive syringe force on the V1 filter stack, so manual delivery became pump-driven dosing, improving the coefficient of variation from 7.41 to 1.95 per cent. More Happy Farm said plainly that not every farmer wants to own a device, which pushed them to a service model — and after a 195-person demonstration found high perceived confidence, the team separated device status from safety judgement in the interface because confidence is not accuracy.","chips":["HongKong-JSS","High School","Score 4","Non-expert changed hardware"]},{"kicker":"Method that nobody rewarded","title":"The only team that defined what 'closed' means","body":"Madrid-UCM built a five-rung integration ladder with an explicit closure criterion: a loop counts as closed only when the revised design goes back to the person whose input triggered it and their response produces a further change. They then demonstrated it on materials — Carmen Garcia Payo and Loreto Garcia Fernandez proposed core-shell capsules, the team built them but could not see the internal structure, took that problem back to the same researchers, and got magnetite as an optical tracer plus cryosectioning, which became a wall-thickness and leakage pipeline. Aurelio Hidalgo's point that a single-use biocatalyst is neither economical nor recoverable killed both placeholder designs and moved the enzyme panel onto a reusable solid support. They also document a change they chose not to make, on the grounds that not adding a pathway is a design decision too. No Best IHP nomination.","chips":["Madrid-UCM","Undergrad","Score 4","Not nominated"]},{"kicker":"Format that mostly did not work","title":"The survey that changes your vocabulary","body":"Large public surveys are the most common instrument in the cohort and the least consequential for design. HFI's 434 responses replaced 'genetically modified' with 'engineered' across all materials and rebuilt the education from basics. Peking's 539 respondents named three priorities the team concedes already outlined the finished project. UCAS-China's 419 public respondents and HongKong-HS's 420 produced awareness statistics and workshop plans. The honest version is GHCIS, which found that its price and speed questions branched into samples too small to use and explicitly refused to convert 'within RMB 30' into a product requirement, carrying it forward as a question for frontline users instead.","chips":["HFI","Peking","GHCIS","UCAS-China","Vocabulary, not vector"]}],"table":{"head":["Team","Section","Score","What changed"],"rows":[["ABOA","Overgrad","4","Purified enzymes dropped for whole cells on carriers; reactor moved to a side stream"],["Al-Nahrain-IRAQ","Undergrad","4","AI model abandoned for equation-based modelling; lab data entry page added"],["Athens","Overgrad","4","Delivery moved from spray to feed; live phage dropped for a non-replicating enzyme"],["BGCFullerton","High School","4","CIF peptides dropped; regolith mixture plan and model validation changed"],["CHINAGuangdongShimen","High School","4","Multivalent antibody replaced by a single monovalent nanobody"],["Cornell","Undergrad","4","Homemade high-voltage supply dropped; hypoxia AND gate added for specificity"],["DTU-Denmark","Overgrad","4","Enzyme step reframed as solvolysis complement; chassis to K. phaffii; docking filter dropped"],["ETH-Zurich","Overgrad","4","Pivot off the Drosophila biopesticide; split-cargo dual targeting invented"],["Eton-College-UK","High School","4","Plasmid backbone changed; reusable reader plus disposable cartridge fixed"],["GCGS","High School","4","VOC module de-scoped; temperature kill switch added, pH switch declined with a reason"],["GEMS-Taiwan","High School","4","Sensing moved out of the cell; perfusion reactor added; proline delivery abandoned"],["GYHS","High School","4","Bond strength replaced by a seven-part requirement set; V2 handling redesigned"],["HFI","High School","4","Lysine-responsive promoter abandoned for constitutive expression"],["HK-Joint-School","High School","4","Goal shifted from fire retardancy to non-toxic, low-smoke; benchmark added"],["HKSSC","High School","4","Kill switch and controlled use; MIC/growth-rate design; pH range from regulator data"],["HKU-HongKong","Unlisted","4","Hypothesis narrowed to partial inflammation modulation; M1/M2 framing dropped"],["HUST-China","Undergrad","4","Reflectin module abandoned entirely for a fashion-waste cellulose route"],["HangzhouFourteenAP","High School","4","Target moved from mineralised calculus to pre-mineralisation biofilm matrix"],["Heidelberg","Undergrad","4","Expression host swapped to a Serratia cassette; engineering retargeted onto GvpC"],["HongKong-HS","High School","4","Toehold switch replaced by HCR; ThT fluorescence replaced by G4/hemin colour"],["HongKong-JSS","High School","4","Colour sensor replaced by spectrometer; syringe replaced by pump dosing"],["Hongwen School","High School","4","IBS claims struck; selection marker changed; near-site processing made a hard constraint"],["ICJFLS","High School","4","Capsule killed for mouthwash/lozenge/gum set; plasmid dropped for chromosomal integration"],["IISER-Kolkata","Unlisted","4","Kill switch rebuilt around a hypochlorite sensor because plants do not use UV"],["KAUST-KSA","Overgrad","4","Dsup added to the chassis; payload reprioritised by real mission conditions"],["LYON","Undergrad","4","All living cells removed from the filter; households ruled out as customers"],["Lambert-GA","High School","4","Nanobodies abandoned for minibinders; target narrowed to the VP3 P-domain"],["MIT-MAHE","Undergrad","4","Target customer moved from fragrance houses to aroma compound manufacturers"],["Madrid-UCM","Undergrad","4","Secretion and consortium killed for immobilised enzymes; containment above performance"],["Marburg","Overgrad","4","5'UTR redesigned so the PPR site and RBS are disconnected; RBS testing dropped"],["McGill","Undergrad","4","Dropped ultra-purification; feedstock moved to fresh tailings; tolling business model"],["McMaster-Canada","Undergrad","4","Oncology and allergy concepts dropped for localised gut-associated systems"],["Muenster-University","Overgrad","4","Prediction pipeline rebuilt with a geometric scoring layer; NLR route dropped"],["NBJF","High School","4","DNA storage device abandoned for the enzymatic-writing bottleneck"],["NFLSHS-CHINA","High School","4","Two plasmids collapsed into one; aqueous formulation killed for oil and capsule"],["NJU-China","Undergrad","4","Recorded associations split from model predictions in every view"],["NUS-Singapore","Undergrad","4","Primary use moved from industrial monitoring to early-stage R&D"],["NYCU-Taiwan","Undergrad","4","Claimed advantages withdrawn after reading a competitor's documentation"],["Oxford","Undergrad","4","Living symbiont chassis dropped for heat-inactivated yeast, with the cost published"],["PSI Korea","High School","4","Auto-exposure disabled and imaging conditions fixed; instrument separated from material"],["Princeton","Undergrad","4","AlphaFold3 cut from the pipeline; IL-6 and amyloid-beta targets dropped"],["QingdaoAcademy","High School","4","One-pot process split in two; pH switch abandoned; desalting and endotoxin control added"],["RDFZ-China","High School","4","Host switched to C41(DE3); metal anchors replaced by on-site stone"],["SEHS","High School","4","Indication moved from liver to gastric cancer; binding re-tested per format"],["SMS-Shenzhen","High School","4","Target customer relocated from front-end recyclers to hydrometallurgical tail streams"],["SUIS-SFLS","High School","4","Deliverable rewritten from finished dressing to characterised protein plus QC records"],["Stanford University","Undergrad","4","Burns dropped for keloids; target moved from prevention to established scars"],["Stockholm","Overgrad","4","Open release abandoned for a sealed reactor sited at the membrane-bioreactor stage"],["TAU-Israel","Overgrad","4","Markers stratified across superficial and deep lesions; biosensor demoted to triage"],["TU Delft","Overgrad","4","Antibiotics dropped for AMPs; pre-coated implant instead of in-theatre paste"],["UAlberta","Undergrad","4","Binding-pocket release abandoned; yeast dropped for E. coli; GFP to mScarlet"],["UCAS-China","Undergrad","4","NKX2-1 cargo dropped for SLPI; repositioned to asthma maintenance"],["UCNZ","Undergrad","4","Distributed plants dropped for one central facility; sustainability claim narrowed"],["UFABC-Brazil","Overgrad","4","Pipetted cell-free reaction replaced by a paper strip; alert routed to a support network"],["UNILausanne","Overgrad","4","Defend strategy kept against the model's own advice; model scope declared the limit"],["UOttawa","Undergrad","4","Target stream moved from bitumen to diesel; pH loop added to the P&ID"],["UZurich","Overgrad","4","Machine-learning plan dropped for established software; root cohesion added to the model"],["Uni-Padua-IT","Undergrad","4","Cold-tolerance module cut; perchlorate genes compartmentalised in heterocysts"],["Vilnius-Lithuania","Undergrad","4","Gel software moved off image classification onto band-distance matching"],["WUXI-DSAS","High School","4","gtdT excised to restore linearity; output changed to a creatinine ratio"],["WageningenUR","Overgrad","4","Biosensor and capture modules created; readout changed to released fluoride"],["William-and-Mary","Undergrad","4","Readout replaced by CFU viability; seawater microcosm experiments added"],["Worldshaper-Shanghai","High School","4","Capacity-building dropped for licensing; sunlight-is-greener claims deleted"],["XJTLU-China","Undergrad","4","Success redefined as soluble protein, not total expression"],["ASIJ-Tokyo","High School","3","Positioning moved from replacement to extra source; patch route added"],["Baltimore","High School","3","Preservation study and patent strategy added; changes peripheral to the build"],["CalPolySLO","Undergrad","3","Survivability testing and a misuse framework added; the build itself unchanged"],["DKU","Undergrad","3","Per-application immunogenicity thresholds and clearer tool output; attribution collective"],["GHCIS","High School","3","Microfluidic format replaced by filter paper, on unnamed industry advice"],["GU Frankfurt","Overgrad","3","Binder accuracy made the governing constraint; biggest change was procedural"],["Kyoto","Undergrad","3","Food themes abandoned and the question reframed; specific changes not itemised"],["Peking","Undergrad","3","Broad-spectrum pesticide and crude biocontrol routes dropped; chain not attributed"],["SDU-Denmark","Overgrad","3","Target moved to reliable low-power generation; no named source"],["SJTU-BioX-Shanghai","Undergrad","3","Repositioned as a post-debridement dressing with physical containment; sources unnamed"],["Toronto","Overgrad","3","Contained bioreactor and close-homology enzymes preferred; stakeholders unnamed"],["UCL","Undergrad","3","Regulatory gap found and a techno-economic model built; the device did not change"],["UPF-Barcelona","Undergrad","3","Central claim shrunk from bulk soil water to a hydration shell at the root"],["ZJU-China","Undergrad","3","Cost weighted more heavily in material design; attribution aggregated"],["ZQT-Nanjing","High School","3","Narrowed from general skincare to barrier repair after a 397-person survey"],["BAID-China","High School","2","Communication depth differentiated by audience; accessibility artefacts revised"],["BNDS-China","High School","2","Workflow discipline borrowed from a peer team; rest is framing"],["BOKU-Vienna","Overgrad","2","Claims key design decisions changed but does not say which"],["CAU-China","Undergrad","2","Need reported from Malawi and Zambia; no design consequence recorded"],["GreatBay-SCIE","High School","2","Slogan changed on stigma grounds; design philosophy only loosely attributed"],["HBUT-China","Undergrad","2","Named virologist fed the risk assessment; no design consequence stated"],["Jilin-China","Undergrad","2","Double-loop reframing of what counts as success; consequences not shown"],["KIT","Overgrad","2","Survey converted into two inclusivity deliverables; science untouched"],["Labi-Taiwan","High School","2","Complements-not-replaces framing and a detects-not-diagnoses statement"],["Mingdao","High School","2","Five honest questions, including a no-project condition; no design change recorded"],["UMA Malaga","Undergrad","2","Question reframed around the diagnostic pathway, not the device"],["UOregon","Overgrad","2","Plant operators confirmed the gap; equity framing shaped, design did not"],["NIS Almaty-Medeu","High School","1","Questions published in advance; no answers or consequences recorded yet"],["Yucai-SZ","High School","1","A 719-response survey tested the premise; no consequence recorded"]]},"method":"Every team in this report is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee, so this is the most decorated tenth of the competition and not a representative sample. Read '64 of 93 closed the loop' as 'closing the loop is normal among teams that win things', not as a statement about iGEM at large. Every team file with any good.ihp content was scored on the four-point rubric from what the file itself states: a 4 required a named stakeholder, a specific thing said, and a change to the build, the deployment, the readout, the safety design or the business model that the file ties to that input. Teams whose only documented consequence was a change of framing, language, education material or evidence package scored 2 or 3 however elaborately the process was branded, and awards were ignored throughout. The rubric cannot verify that a change was made because of the advice rather than attributed to it afterwards, cannot see the wiki behind the summary, and cannot distinguish a thin causal chain from a thin write-up of a thick one. Files continued to land while the scoring ran; all 93 present at the end were read and scored, so the set is complete as of writing but not closed.","scored":93},{"id":"technique-census","tab":"drylab","kicker":"Original analysis","title":"What 2026's best teams actually reached for","title_zh":"2026 年最強的團隊，實際上用了什麼","lede":"A census of the computational tools named across every team file in this report — and the one habit that separates the podium from everybody else.","lede_zh":"對本報告所有團隊檔案中提及的運算工具所做的普查——以及把頒獎台和其他人分開的那一個習慣。","body":"Across the team files gathered here, **AlphaFold is still the default**: it is named by roughly a third of teams, more than any other modelling tool, and more than twice as often as the open successors. Boltz appears in a handful of files, ESMFold in a handful more, RFdiffusion and ProteinMPNN in fewer still. The academic literature has already moved past this — open models now match or beat the gated flagship — but iGEM has not caught up. That lag is an opportunity: a team that works fluently with the current open stack is doing something most of the competition is not.\n\nThe second pattern is that **the dedicated systems-biology tools have quietly lost**. COPASI, once the standard way an iGEM team built a kinetic model, appears in one file. Tellurium appears in one. MATLAB holds on in four. Everything else is Python — named by more teams than any other single item in the census, usually SciPy integrating an ODE system written by hand. Teaching COPASI as the entry point to modelling now teaches a tool the field has left behind.\n\nThe third pattern is the surprise. **Techno-economic analysis — costing the thing, modelling unit economics — is done by more high-school teams than undergraduate teams**, in absolute numbers as well as proportionally. High-school teams are being pushed hard on implementation and business thinking, and they are delivering it. Meanwhile GROMACS, full molecular dynamics, appears exclusively in undergraduate files and never once in a high-school file. The two tiers are not weaker and stronger versions of each other; they are differently shaped.\n\n**Then the finding that matters.** We checked which teams do both halves of modelling properly: fit the model to their own measured data (parameter estimation, regression, R², RMSE, confidence intervals, error bars) *and* validate it against something held back (held-out data, cross-validation, a separate experimental test). Only 14 of 54 teams do both.\n\nOf those 14, **10 are Top 10 teams — 71%**. Of the 42 that do not close that loop, 17 are Top 10 — **40%**. Every one of the four who closed the loop without reaching a Top 10 won a major special prize anyway: XJTLU-China and Jilin-China in Best Model, NJU-China took Best Software & AI Project, Vilnius-Lithuania was nominated in three categories.\n\nThis is the single most actionable number in the report. Not which model you use — whether you close the loop between the model and your own data. It is also, conveniently, the cheapest capability to build: it needs no GPU, no licence and no collaboration. It needs a student who knows what a residual is.","body_zh":"在本報告蒐集的團隊檔案中，**AlphaFold 仍然是預設選項**：約三分之一的團隊提到它，比任何其他建模工具都多，也超過開源後繼者的兩倍以上。Boltz 出現在少數幾份檔案，ESMFold 再多一點，RFdiffusion 與 ProteinMPNN 更少。學術文獻早已走過這一步——開源模型現已可匹敵甚至超越封閉的旗艦模型——但 iGEM 還沒跟上。這個時間差就是機會：能熟練運用當前開源工具鏈的團隊，正在做大多數競爭者沒做的事。\n\n第二個型態是，**專用的系統生物學工具已悄悄落敗**。COPASI 曾經是 iGEM 團隊建立動力學模型的標準做法，如今只出現在一份檔案中。Tellurium 一份。MATLAB 勉強守住四份。其餘全是 Python——在整份普查中被提及的團隊數多於任何單一項目，通常是用 SciPy 積分一組手寫的 ODE 系統。現在把 COPASI 當作建模的入門，等於是在教一個領域已經放下的工具。\n\n第三個型態令人意外。**做技術經濟分析——計算成本、建立單位經濟模型——的高中隊伍比大學部隊伍還多**，絕對數與比例皆然。高中組被大力要求落實應用與商業思考，而他們做到了。相對地，完整的分子動力學（GROMACS）只出現在大學部的檔案中，高中組一次也沒有。這兩個層級不是同一件事的強弱版本，它們的形狀本來就不同。\n\n**接著是真正重要的發現。** 我們檢查了哪些團隊把建模的兩半都做完：以自己量到的資料擬合模型（參數估計、回歸、R²、RMSE、信賴區間、誤差棒），*並且*用保留的資料驗證它（held-out 資料、交叉驗證、獨立的實驗測試）。54 支團隊中只有 14 支兩者皆備。\n\n這 14 支裡，**有 10 支是 Top 10 團隊——71%**。而在沒有閉合這個迴圈的 42 支中，只有 17 支進入 Top 10——**40%**。閉合了迴圈卻未進 Top 10 的那四支，無一例外都拿下了重要特別獎：XJTLU-China 與 Jilin-China 在最佳模型，NJU-China 拿下最佳軟體與 AI 專案，Vilnius-Lithuania 則獲三項提名。\n\n這是整份報告中最可執行的一個數字。重點不是你用哪個模型，而是你有沒有把模型與自己的資料之間的迴圈閉合起來。而且它恰好也是最便宜的能力：不需要 GPU、不需要授權、不需要合作對象。它需要的是一位知道什麼叫殘差的學生。","cards":[{"kicker":"The headline number","title":"71% versus 40%","title_zh":"71% 對 40%","body":"Teams that both fit their model to their own data and validated it against something held back reached a Top 10 at 71%. Teams that did not reached it at 40%. Note the sample is already decorated — every team here is a Top 10 or special-prize team — so this is loop-closure separating winners from other winners, not from the general field.","body_zh":"既以自身資料擬合模型、又用保留資料加以驗證的團隊，進入 Top 10 的比例是 71%；沒有這麼做的則是 40%。請注意樣本本身已經過篩選——這裡每一支團隊都是 Top 10 或特別獎隊伍——因此這是「閉合迴圈」把贏家從其他贏家中分出來，而不是從一般參賽者中分出來。","chips":["14 of 54 closed the loop","10 of those 14 made Top 10"]},{"kicker":"Still the default","title":"AlphaFold has not been displaced inside iGEM","title_zh":"在 iGEM 裡，AlphaFold 還沒被取代","body":"Roughly a third of teams name AlphaFold, more than twice the rate of Boltz, ESMFold, RFdiffusion or ProteinMPNN. The research literature moved to the open stack over the past year; the competition has not. The teams already working in Boltz and the MPNN family — Lambert-GA, Heidelberg, GU Frankfurt, DTU-Denmark, Princeton — are visibly ahead of the curve rather than merely current.","body_zh":"約三分之一的團隊提到 AlphaFold，是 Boltz、ESMFold、RFdiffusion 或 ProteinMPNN 的兩倍以上。研究文獻在過去一年已轉向開源工具鏈，競賽卻還沒。已經在用 Boltz 與 MPNN 家族的隊伍——Lambert-GA、Heidelberg、GU Frankfurt、DTU-Denmark、Princeton——明顯走在前面，而不只是跟上。","chips":["AlphaFold ×19","Boltz ×7","ProteinMPNN ×7","RFdiffusion ×3"]},{"kicker":"A tool generation ended","title":"Python ate the modelling stack","title_zh":"Python 吃掉了整個建模工具鏈","body":"COPASI appears once. Tellurium once. MATLAB four times. Python appears in more team files than any other item in the census, usually SciPy integrating a hand-written ODE system, with scikit-learn behind it for anything statistical. For a programme deciding what to teach, this settles the question: teach Python and the numerical stack, and treat SBML-based tools as an interchange format rather than a starting point.","body_zh":"COPASI 出現一次，Tellurium 一次，MATLAB 四次。Python 出現在比普查中任何其他項目都多的團隊檔案裡，通常是用 SciPy 積分手寫的 ODE 系統，統計部分則交給 scikit-learn。對一個正在決定要教什麼的課程而言，這已經定案：教 Python 與數值運算工具鏈，把以 SBML 為基礎的工具當作交換格式，而不是起點。","chips":["Python ×31","scikit-learn ×8","COPASI ×1","Tellurium ×1"]},{"kicker":"The inversion","title":"High-school teams cost their projects; undergraduates often don't","title_zh":"高中隊伍會算成本，大學部常常不算","body":"Techno-economic analysis appears in more high-school files than undergraduate ones, both in absolute count and as a share of the tier. Full molecular dynamics runs the other way and is exclusively undergraduate. The tiers are differently shaped rather than simply further apart, and a high-school programme that assumes it must catch up on everything is aiming at the wrong gap.","body_zh":"技術經濟分析在高中組檔案中出現的次數，無論絕對數或組內占比都高於大學部；完整的分子動力學則完全相反，只出現在大學部。兩個層級的形狀不同，而不只是距離遠近的差別。一個假定自己必須在所有面向上追趕的高中課程，瞄錯了缺口。","chips":["Techno-economic: 7 HS vs 5 UG","GROMACS: 6 UG, 0 HS"]},{"kicker":"A weaker result, reported anyway","title":"Publishing your failures: real, but a smaller effect than it looks","title_zh":"公開失敗：效果是真的，但沒有看起來那麼大","body":"Several analysts noticed the same thing independently — Toronto, WageningenUR and UZurich each put a prominent negative or failed result on the wiki, and two of them won the award in that exact category. We tested it across every file. Teams that openly report failure reach a Top 10 at 54%, against 41% for those that do not. That is a real gap, but it is far smaller than the loop-closure gap, and the measurement is partly circular: it detects how candid *our own summary* of a team was, not reliably how candid the team was. Treat it as a reason to publish the negative result, not as proof it wins prizes.","body_zh":"好幾位分析員各自獨立注意到同一件事——Toronto、WageningenUR 與 UZurich 都在 wiki 上顯著地放上了一個負面或失敗的結果，而其中兩隊正是在對應的獎項類別中獲獎。我們對所有檔案做了檢驗：公開報告失敗的團隊進入 Top 10 的比例是 54%，沒有這麼做的則是 41%。差距是真的，但遠小於「閉合迴圈」的差距，而且這個量測帶有循環性：它偵測到的是*我們自己的摘要*有多坦白，而未必能可靠反映團隊有多坦白。請把它當作「應該公開負面結果」的理由，而不是「這樣就會得獎」的證明。","chips":["54% vs 41%","measurement is confounded"]},{"kicker":"What this means for GEMS","title":"The cheapest capability is the one that correlates with winning","title_zh":"最便宜的能力，正好就是和得獎相關的那一個","body":"Closing the model-data loop needs no GPU, no licence, no partner lab and no new chassis. It needs a student who can fit a curve, report an uncertainty and hold data back for a test. That is a term's teaching, and on this evidence it moves the result more than any tool choice. It is Phase 2 of the roadmap for exactly this reason.","body_zh":"閉合模型與資料之間的迴圈，不需要 GPU、不需要授權、不需要合作實驗室、也不需要新的底盤。它需要的是一位會擬合曲線、會報告不確定度、並且懂得保留資料做測試的學生。那是一個學期的教學量，而根據這些證據，它對結果的影響大於任何工具選擇。這正是它成為路線圖階段二的原因。","chips":["No GPU required","One term of teaching"]}],"method":"Counts come from pattern-matching the `dry` and `good` fields of every team file in this report, not from reading the wikis a second time, so a technique a team used but did not write up is invisible here. The sample is decorated teams only — every file is a Top 10 or special-prize winner or nominee — so the baselines are not the whole competition. The loop-closure test looks for explicit language about fitting, uncertainty and validation; a team that did the work but described it loosely will be undercounted. Read the numbers as a ranking, not a measurement.","method_zh":"計數方式是對本報告每一份團隊檔案的 `dry` 與 `good` 欄位做樣式比對，而非重新閱讀 wiki，因此團隊做了卻沒寫下來的技術在這裡是看不見的。樣本僅限獲獎隊伍——每一份檔案都是 Top 10 或特別獎得主／入圍者——所以基準值並不代表整個競賽。迴圈閉合的判準是尋找明確描述擬合、不確定度與驗證的文字；做了卻寫得含糊的團隊會被低估。請把這些數字當成排序，而不是量測。"}],"roadmap":[{"title":"Phase 1 · Make the current work reproducible","title_zh":"階段一 · 讓現有工作可重現","when":"0–3 months","when_zh":"0–3 個月","lede":"Before building anything new, make what already exists survivable by the next cohort.","lede_zh":"在建造新東西之前，先讓既有成果能被下一屆接手。","items":["**Put every analysis in version control.** One GEMS Research GitHub organisation, one repository per project, with the raw data, the notebook and the figure-generating script in the same place. If a figure cannot be regenerated from the repository, it does not count as a result.","**Write down the measurement protocols.** Calibration standards, units, replicate counts, how uncertainty was computed. The 2026 Best Measurement teams all did this; it is the cheapest credibility a dry lab can buy.","**Standardise the environment.** One `environment.yml` or `requirements.txt` per project, Python 3.12+, pinned versions. A student should be able to clone and run in under ten minutes.","**Archive the 2026 ReLEAF dry lab properly** — the OD600 signal processing, the optogenetic circuit model, the hardware firmware — as the first entry in the institutional record.","**Write the one-page biosecurity and ordering policy.** The US National Policy for Nucleic Acid Synthesis Screening (November 2026) now ties federal funding to buying synthetic DNA only from certified providers that screen orders of 50+ nucleotides. Mirror it: certified suppliers only, a documented internal review of any sequence design, an explicit scope statement excluding pathogen and toxin sequences, signed by every student before their first order. It costs an afternoon and it is the first thing a serious partner asks about."],"items_zh":["**把所有分析放進版本控制。** 一個 GEMS Research GitHub organisation，一個專案一個 repository，原始資料、notebook 與產生圖表的腳本放在同一處。若一張圖無法從 repository 重新產生，它就不算結果。","**寫下量測流程。** 校正標準品、單位、重複次數、不確定度如何計算。2026 年所有最佳量測獎團隊都做到了這點；這是乾實驗室能買到最便宜的可信度。","**統一環境。** 每個專案一份 `environment.yml` 或 `requirements.txt`，Python 3.12 以上，版本鎖定。學生應該能在十分鐘內 clone 下來就跑起來。","**妥善歸檔 2026 ReLEAF 的乾實驗室成果** —— OD600 訊號處理、光遺傳電路模型、硬體韌體 —— 作為機構紀錄的第一筆。","**寫下一頁的生物安全與訂購政策。** 美國《核酸合成篩查國家政策》（2026 年 11 月）已將聯邦經費與「只向通過認證、且會篩查 50 個核苷酸以上訂單的供應商購買合成 DNA」綁在一起。比照辦理：僅限認證供應商、任何序列設計都要有書面內部審查、明確排除病原與毒素序列，並由每位學生在第一次下單前簽署。這只需要一個下午，而且是認真的合作對象第一個會問的事。"],"outcome":"A new student can reproduce any 2026 figure from the repository alone, without asking anybody.","outcome_zh":"新進學生只靠 repository 就能重現 2026 年的任何一張圖，不需要問任何人。"},{"title":"Phase 2 · Build the core modelling skill","title_zh":"階段二 · 建立核心建模能力","when":"3–9 months","when_zh":"3–9 個月","lede":"Two tracks, taught deliberately, with a real deliverable at the end of each.","lede_zh":"兩條軌道，刻意教學，每條都有真實的產出。","items":["**Track A — dynamical systems.** ODE models of genetic circuits, parameter fitting to the team's own data, sensitivity analysis, identifiability. Tools: Python with SciPy and lmfit, Tellurium/COPASI for the SBML side. Deliverable: a circuit model fitted to real GEMS time-course data, with confidence intervals on every parameter.","**Track B — structural and sequence modelling.** Structure prediction is now free infrastructure: the open models (Boltz-2, Chai-1, OpenFold3, ColabFold) match or beat the gated flagship, so folding a protein is a commodity step, not a project. Put one shared GPU box or a modest cloud budget behind an internal queue, make \"fold it, then read the confidence metrics\" compulsory in every project, and teach the hard part — knowing when pLDDT and PAE are lying to you. Deliverable: a designed or selected variant with a documented computational rationale, taken to the bench.","**Teach uncertainty before teaching models.** Error propagation, replicate design, what a fit actually claims. Most student models fail here, not at the mathematics.","**Run a weekly dry-lab clinic.** One hour, somebody presents a figure, everyone else attacks it. This is how modelling taste transmits between cohorts."],"items_zh":["**軌道 A —— 動力系統。** 基因電路的 ODE 模型、以自身資料擬合參數、敏感度分析、可辨識性。工具：Python 搭配 SciPy 與 lmfit，SBML 端使用 Tellurium/COPASI。產出：一個以 GEMS 真實時間序列資料擬合的電路模型，每個參數都附信賴區間。","**軌道 B —— 結構與序列建模。** 結構預測現在已是免費的基礎設施：開源模型（Boltz-2、Chai-1、OpenFold3、ColabFold）已可匹敵甚至超越封閉的旗艦模型，因此「把蛋白質折出來」是一個標準步驟，而不是一個專案。配置一台共用 GPU 主機或一筆適度的雲端預算，架一個內部排程佇列，規定每個專案都必須「先折、再讀信心指標」，並教真正困難的部分——判斷 pLDDT 與 PAE 什麼時候在騙你。產出：一個經過設計或篩選的變體，附上完整的運算理由，並實際進到實驗檯。","**先教不確定度，再教模型。** 誤差傳遞、重複設計、一次擬合究竟主張了什麼。多數學生模型敗在這裡，而不是數學。","**每週一次乾實驗室診療會。** 一小時，一個人報一張圖，其他人負責挑戰它。建模的品味就是這樣在屆與屆之間傳下去的。"],"outcome":"Two or three students who can independently build, fit and defend a model — and who can teach the next two or three.","outcome_zh":"有兩三位學生能獨立建立、擬合並為自己的模型辯護——並且能教會下兩三位。"},{"title":"Phase 3 · Ship one tool the outside world uses","title_zh":"階段三 · 做出一個外界真的會用的工具","when":"9–18 months","when_zh":"9–18 個月","lede":"The difference between a competition team and a research centre is whether anybody outside uses what you built.","lede_zh":"競賽團隊與研究中心的差別，在於外界有沒有人用你做的東西。","items":["**Commit to the Bacillus optogenetics line.** Both trend reviews independently pointed here. Port and properly characterise a CcaS/CcaR or LOV-based light-inducible cassette in *B. subtilis* with full dose-response, dynamic range and growth-stage characterisation. In a twelve-paper literature that is on its own a publishable contribution, and it is the natural continuation of ReLEAF rather than a fresh start.","**Pick one narrow, real problem** that GEMS has genuine data on — the strongest candidate is the optogenetic induction and OD600 measurement work from ReLEAF, where GEMS already has instrumentation, data and a Best Measurement award behind it.","**Build it as a deployed web tool, not a notebook.** Documented, licensed, with example data, a DOI, and a URL anybody can open. Teams that only publish source code get used by nobody.","**Design for other people's data from day one.** Input format, validation, error messages. This is the single most common failure in iGEM software.","**Get three outside users and write down what broke.** Other Taiwanese schools, a university lab, a 2027 iGEM team. Their complaints are the roadmap for version two."],"items_zh":["**確立枯草桿菌光遺傳學這條路線。** 兩份趨勢分析各自獨立地指向這裡。在 *B. subtilis* 中移植並完整表徵一組 CcaS/CcaR 或 LOV 型的光誘導卡匣，做出完整的劑量反應、動態範圍與生長期表徵。在一個只有十二篇文獻的領域裡，光是這件事本身就足以發表，而且這是 ReLEAF 的自然延伸，不是重新開始。","**挑一個狹窄而真實的問題**，而且 GEMS 手上有真正的資料——最強的候選是 ReLEAF 的光遺傳誘導與 OD600 量測工作，GEMS 已經有儀器、有資料，背後還有一座最佳量測獎。","**把它做成已部署的網頁工具，而不是 notebook。** 有文件、有授權、有範例資料、有 DOI，以及任何人都能打開的網址。只釋出原始碼的團隊，沒有人會用。","**從第一天就為別人的資料設計。** 輸入格式、驗證、錯誤訊息。這是 iGEM 軟體最常見的單一失敗原因。","**找到三位外部使用者，並記錄哪裡壞了。** 其他台灣學校、一間大學實驗室、一支 2027 iGEM 團隊。他們的抱怨就是第二版的路線圖。"],"outcome":"A tool with a URL, a licence, documentation and users who are not GEMS students.","outcome_zh":"一個有網址、有授權、有文件，而且使用者不是 GEMS 學生的工具。"},{"title":"Phase 4 · Become a place other people come to","title_zh":"階段四 · 成為別人會來的地方","when":"18 months +","when_zh":"18 個月以上","lede":"Institutional standing comes from being useful to people who owe you nothing.","lede_zh":"機構地位來自於：對那些不欠你任何東西的人仍然有用。","items":["**Run a dry-lab school for Taiwanese iGEM and high-school teams.** Modelling, measurement, reproducibility. Teaching forces the material to become transmissible, and it builds the network that later supplies collaborators.","**Publish.** A methods paper, a preprint, or a well-documented dataset. One citable artefact per year changes how every later conversation starts.","**Keep a standing partnership with a university lab and a non-academic stakeholder** — a farm, a clinic, a municipal body. The stakeholder relationship is what makes human practices real rather than performed, and it is the thing competition teams cannot build in nine months.","**Maintain the trend watch.** This report should be regenerated at least twice a year; the academic and industry tabs are built to be re-run."],"items_zh":["**為台灣的 iGEM 與高中團隊辦一所乾實驗室學校。** 建模、量測、可重現性。教學會逼迫內容變得可傳遞，也建立起日後提供合作者的人脈網絡。","**發表。** 一篇方法論文、一份預印本，或一套文件完整的資料集。每年一個可被引用的產物，會改變此後每一次對話的起點。","**與一間大學實驗室和一個非學術利害關係人維持長期夥伴關係** —— 一座農場、一間診所、一個地方機關。利害關係人關係是讓人類實踐成為真實而非表演的關鍵，也是競賽團隊在九個月內建立不起來的東西。","**持續追蹤趨勢。** 這份報告每年至少重新生成兩次；學術與產業頁就是為了可重跑而設計的。"],"outcome":"GEMS Research is cited, invited and asked for help by people who were never GEMS students.","outcome_zh":"GEMS Research 被從未是 GEMS 學生的人引用、邀請並尋求協助。"}]};
